  "final_message": "I wrote `answer.json` with four functions that emit `subscription.updated` directly:\n\n- `subscriptions.transition` emits it for every status change except a move to `canceled`, which emits `subscription.canceled` instead.\n- `subscriptions.change_items` emits it after the items are swapped.\n- `subscriptions.cancel` emits it when the cancellation is scheduled for period end.\n- `subscriptions.reactivate` emits it when it clears a scheduled cancellation.\n\n`pause` and `resume` also produce the event, but only through `transition`, so I left them out. I didn't open `resume` or `advance_period` in full; a search for `emit(` across the package found no other `subscription.updated` call. Nothing else writes to `ctx.store.events` except `emit` itself. I didn't run the tests.",
